#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133464 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "816d35ed-007d-58b9-9c59-16302359e658" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Angle With a Given Measure"}] :question/id #uuid "deb87162-187a-5f89-9157-b84b5d8178f7" :question/math-academy-id "e-10592" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5ef5c74898174a3c6119eac325c3158b227a9cfc967326298f56c14f891b6bea.png)\n\nWhich angle has a measure of $90^{\\circ}$?" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the angle with a measure $90^\\circ$ on our diagram.\n\n![](images/85/859dda507ff6f983a091ecdbf62e01d27230bb210626232388fd344c3e194a8c.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the angle $\\angle{COD}$ (or $\\angle{DOC}$) has a measure of $90^\\circ$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133465 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133910 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "773c6135-d786-593d-8fa6-92e929904554" :knowledge-point/title "Reading the Measure of an Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "5df19497-b07f-57e3-9589-a488291147bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-10600" :question/problem "![](images/f0/f00f3f66717f230fb42264ca5a0873b394ea1d86002f00517062287f8983f236.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of the angle $\\angle{NRP}$?" :question/worked-solution "If we trace along the letters of the angle name, from $N$ to $R$ to $P$, we can see the angle $\\angle{NRP}$.\n\n![](images/1a/1a9498bf166c686b8c2e5c3017aeb8625cf36c35d20069f5eb82adcc5c797fa8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nm\\angle{NRP}=110^\\circ\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133540 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133970 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7eff006-e868-5994-a895-708ff74808b4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Angles Using Angle Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "ebc8ba04-2c55-56bd-b07c-f5f95d0841c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-2584" :question/problem "Which numbered angle refers to the same angle as $\\widehat{GHA}$?\n\n![](images/47/47841a386b57f8615897cb73b1b98f15e975c78722f29d8baca92e7c7663a527.png)" :question/worked-solution "If we trace along the letters of the angle name, from $G$ to $H$ to $A$, we see that $\\widehat{GHA}$ refers to the angle $\\angle 3$.\n\n![](images/10/100349e33233f2152ce236be2d17dc2fe3a59035a88336e26554eb6864d6059a.png)\n\nTherefore, $\\angle{3}$ is another name for $\\widehat{GHA}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134120 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "816d35ed-007d-58b9-9c59-16302359e658" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Angle With a Given Measure"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90c33e63-be24-5fee-bac2-d314cbf69b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "COD^(^)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130877} {:answer/id #uuid "a290a323-62c7-5298-b531-7abdbed67125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "AOD^(^)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130878} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb78057-903b-5bae-96c8-3546a5568229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "AOB^(^)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130879} {:answer/id #uuid "de53b034-20d6-5c65-bbe5-09df5963f3f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "BOD^(^)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130880} {:answer/id #uuid "388a84f3-e2f1-58dd-bbd8-52d6d91d66ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "BOC^(^)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130881}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4d91f790-cdad-5b43-976a-ae7e27bf9baa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130876}] :question/id #uuid "d2107a33-4f8b-533f-ae6c-505eca3a5d96" :question/math-academy-id "q-150809" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd5841753edf7b3d2b0008057777e0b0338f54d3188c398bbc85d9c897d6ea64.png)\n\nWhich angle has a measure o